  "evidence_notes": "Rachel, 36, was diagnosed with Crohn's at 33 after years of misdiagnosis. She also has asthma and rheumatoid arthritis. She tried mesalamine, prednisone, and azathioprine, all with limited success or adverse effects. She initially resisted biologics due to needle phobia but eventually started Entyvio infusions. It worked well for a year, but she then developed joint pain, leading to an RA diagnosis. She added methotrexate for RA. Entyvio is losing effectiveness, and she is considering Stelara. Her overall outcome is ongoing as she manages multiple conditions and anticipates a treatment switch."
